/*
:name: arr_comb_tmp
:type: equiv
:verilog_top: arr_comb_tmp
:pyrope_top: arr_comb_tmp
:state_pair_gap: mems=0/1
*/
// A blocking temp feeding a comb-array store (`t = d; arr[0] = t`).
//
// This .prp is the VERBATIM `lhd compile arr_comb_tmp.v --emit-dir pyrope:`
// output (headers added).
//
// USED TO FAIL (fixed 2026-07-27, lhdsuite fixme.md 1h). The emission read
// `mut t = 0 … t = 0ub? … arr[0] = t`: the `t = d` assignment was lost and the
// store took the declaration poison. It was NOT a slang->LNAST drop, as this
// comment used to claim — the defect was in `upass.ssa`, which copied a
// >=3-child (tuple_set) store VERBATIM and so left its VALUE operand on the
// stale base name while the def had been renamed to `t___ssa_1`. constprop then
// folded the base to its declaration value and DCE deleted the real write.
// `upass_ssa.cpp` now routes such a store through the same
// target-verbatim/operands-renamed path as tuple_get/tuple_add/attr_*, and `t`
// collapses into the store as it should.
//
// SOUNDNESS TRAP worth keeping: while it was broken the dropped assignment left
// a don't-care, so the native cvc5 `lhd lec` of the two lgraphs returned a
// VACUOUS PROVEN — only the yosys-referenced lgcheck flows (equiv, v2prp2v) saw the
// bug at all. A PROVEN means nothing unless the comparison is sensitive to the
// signal in question.
pub comb arr_comb_tmp::[timecheck=false](sel:u1, d:u1) -> (o:u1) {
  mut arr:[2]u1 = 0
  o = 0ub?
  arr[0] = d
  arr[1] = (~d) & 1
  o = arr[sel]
}
